<title>USA: Hughes electonics eyes sale of two businesses.</title>
<headline>Hughes electonics eyes sale of two businesses.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hughes Electronics Corp, a unit of General Motors Corp is seeking bids for its defense and aerospace businesses, which together could command roughly $8 billion, The Wall Street Journal reported Thursday.</p>
<p>McDonnell Douglas Corp, Northrop Grumman Corp and Raytheon Co are expected to be potential bidders in what is likely to be a highly contested auction, the story says.</p>
